# Frontend i18n (AWT)

Stack: `i18next` + `react-i18next`. Locales: **`es`** (default) and **`en`**. Registry: `apps/web/src/shared/i18n/resources.ts`.

## Hexagonal boundary (mandatory)

| Layer | i18n allowed? |
|-------|----------------|
| `domain/` | **No** — no strings, no `t()`, no locale files |
| `application/` | **No** — use-cases return codes/errors; UI maps to copy |
| `adapters/` | **No** user-facing copy (map API errors to codes/keys at presentation) |
| `presentation/` | **Yes** — only place for feature translation files and `useTranslation` |
| `shared/components` / kit | **Yes** — only via `common` (or a dedicated shared namespace), not feature namespaces |

UI copy lives at the edge. Domain speaks codes; presentation speaks language.

## Where files live

### Feature / page modules (default)

Colocate under the **presentation** folder of the feature (or the parent page slice that owns the UI):

```
modules/<scope>/<feature>/presentation/i18n/
  es.ts
  en.ts
  index.ts

auth/presentation/<screen>/i18n/
  es.ts
  en.ts
  index.ts
```

- One feature namespace → one `presentation/i18n` (or screen folders merged by a parent `presentation/i18n/index.ts`, like auth).
- Shared copy **inside the same feature** (several screens): `presentation/shared/i18n/` then merge in `presentation/i18n/index.ts`.
- Do **not** put feature strings in `shared/i18n/locales/` unless they are truly cross-app.

### Cross-app / kit only

`apps/web/src/shared/i18n/locales/` — `common`, and legacy shared buckets (`settings`, `onboarding`, `calendar`, …) until migrated next to their owners.

- Kit primitives (`shared/components/UI`): prefer props for text **or** `common` keys — never import `comercial` / `auth` into the kit.
- Storybook-only fixtures: `.storybook/i18n.ts` extras, **both** `es` and `en`.

## File shape

```ts
// presentation/i18n/es.ts
export const esFeature = {
  pageTitle: '…',
  saveDraft: '…',
  emptyTitle: '…',
} as const

// presentation/i18n/en.ts
export const enFeature = {
  pageTitle: '…',
  saveDraft: '…',
  emptyTitle: '…',
} as const

// presentation/i18n/index.ts
export { esFeature } from './es'
export { enFeature } from './en'
```

- Export names: `es<Namespace>` / `en<Namespace>` (`esComercial`, `enAuth`, `esAuthLogin`).
- Always `as const`.
- **Same keys** in `es.ts` and `en.ts` — parity required in the same PR.
- Prefer `.ts` objects (typed). JSON only if an existing locale already uses it (e.g. calendar); keep key style consistent.

## Register namespace

Every new feature namespace must be wired in `shared/i18n/resources.ts`:

1. Import `esX` / `enX` from the feature `presentation/i18n`
2. Add under `i18nResources.es` and `i18nResources.en`
3. Append name to `i18nNamespaces`

Namespace name: **camelCase**, short, matches feature (`comercial`, `auth`, `notFound`). One namespace per product area — do not explode into dozens of tiny namespaces without need.

## Key naming

- **camelCase** keys: `loginTitle`, `forcePasswordMismatch`, `mobilePaneActivity`
- Structure by UI concern with prefixes when flat files grow:
  - `…Title` / `…Subtitle` / `…Description`
  - `…Placeholder` / `…Helper` / `…Label`
  - `…Error` / `…Success` / `…Empty`
  - `…Submit` / `…Cancel` (action-specific; reuse `common` for generic Save/Cancel when identical)
- Nested objects OK for large screens (`form: { emailLabel: '…' }`) — access `t('form.emailLabel')`
- **No** locale in the key (`titleEs` forbidden)
- **No** component class names as keys (`AccountStepDrawerTitle` forbidden) — describe meaning, not file
- Interpolation: i18next `{{name}}` — `t('forceOtpSubtitle', { email })`
- Plurals: use i18next plural forms when counts matter (`key_one` / `key_other` or nested plural config) — do not concatenate words in JSX

## Usage in components

```tsx
const { t } = useTranslation('comercial')
const { t: tc } = useTranslation('common')

return <h1>{t('accountInformation')}</h1>
```

- Pass the **namespace** to `useTranslation` — do not dump everything into `common`
- Generic actions (`save`, `cancel`, `loading`, `delete`): `common`
- Feature copy: feature namespace only
- Never hard-code user-facing Spanish/English in JSX/TSX under `presentation/` or kit
- `aria-label`, toast, empty/error CTAs: same rules (see `ux-writing`)
- Do not call `t()` in `domain` / `application` / pure utils used by those layers

## Errors and API messages

- Backend/domain: stable **code** or error type
- Presentation maps code → `t('…Error')`
- Never show raw API/Mongo messages to the user

## Anti-patterns

- Translation files under `domain/`, `application/`, or random `src/locales` for features
- Feature strings only in `shared/i18n/locales/` when a `presentation/` owner exists
- Keys in only one locale
- Hard-coded UI strings in components
- Kit importing feature namespaces
- `t(\`status.${x}\`)` dynamic keys without guaranteeing every `x` exists in both locales
- Duplicating `common.save` inside every feature namespace

## Checklist (new screen / feature copy)

- [ ] Files under owning `presentation/i18n` (or `presentation/<screen>/i18n` + parent merge)
- [ ] `es.ts` + `en.ts` + `index.ts` with identical keys
- [ ] Namespace registered in `resources.ts` + `i18nNamespaces`
- [ ] Components use `useTranslation('<namespace>')`
- [ ] Shared actions from `common` where applicable
- [ ] No i18n leakage into domain/application
- [ ] Storybook: both toolbars `es`/`en` still work (see `storybook-ui-system`)
